questions.q:
Consider the following equation, which represents a reaction in the extraction of chromium from its ore

\begin{aligned}
2 \mathrm{Fe}_{2} \mathrm{O}_{3} \cdot \mathrm{Cr}_{2} \mathrm{O}_{3}+4 \mathrm{Na}_{2} \mathrm{CO}_{3}+3 \mathrm{O}_{2} & \\
\longrightarrow & 2 \mathrm{Fe}_{2} \mathrm{O}_{3}+4 \mathrm{Na}_{2} \mathrm{CrO}_{4}+4 \mathrm{CO}_{2}
\end{aligned}

Which one of the following statements about the oxidation states of the substances is correct?

questions.solution:
 2 \stackrel{+3}{\mathrm{Fe}_{2}} \mathrm{O}_{3} \cdot{ }^{+3} \mathrm{Cr}_{2} \mathrm{O}_{3}+4 \mathrm{Na}_{2} \mathrm{CO}_{3}+3 \mathrm{O}_{2}

\rightarrow 2 \stackrel{+3}{\mathrm{Fe}_{2}} \mathrm{O}_{3}+4 \mathrm{Na}_{2} \stackrel{+6}{\mathrm{Cr} \mathrm{O}_{4}}+4 \mathrm{CO}_{2}

Hence, the oxidation state of chromium increase from $+3$ to $+6$
